{"kind":"assert","text":"AE-1 ruling on ed162ad1: charge the worst case before each call. Add\nno quote and change no namespace protocol.\n\nReason: a charge from an existing bound is never too small, and it\nneeds no new message. A quote is a second exchange that the sender\nalso has to pay for, and it widens the protocol of the stable base.\n\n1. One cost function for each kind of read states the sender's worst\n   case from the bounds that exist: the metadata bound, the 256 KiB\n   declaration and the proof bound. The driver charges through that\n   function before `namespace.births.read` and before\n   `namespace.proofs.read`.\n2. A smaller reply refunds none of that charge. A cached declaration\n   costs the same as a loaded one.\n3. The predicate of ARC-1 calls the same functions, as 2bbd55aa\n   requires. No number is written twice.\n4. State the largest creator chain that the walk admits, and the file\n   and line of that bound. A static test shows that the charge of\n   the largest chain fits the budget of one pass.\n5. State why a walk that the budget refuses succeeds in a later pass.\n   A walk that cannot fit a new budget must not retry without end.\n\nWhen the walk has no bound on the chain, or the largest chain does\nnot fit one pass, stop. Send the numbers in one act before more\nsource. AE-1 adds no cap without a ruling.\n\nA budget refusal in the walk keeps its answer of today. It sends no\npayload and makes no provider call.\n\nThe walk runs before a policy is inserted, so a scope pays it one\ntime for each policy. Say in the note when a scope pays it again.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ed162ad1182144d0b3412687fe0e3772152230dc stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}